<title>JAPAN: Forex rates seem to be stabilising - Sakakibara.</title>
<headline>Forex rates seem to be stabilising - Sakakibara.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Foreign exchange rates seem to be stabilising, senior Finance Ministry official Eisuke Sakakibara told a parliamentary committee on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Movements in currency rates over the past week reflect a gradual penetration in the markets of a strong agreement by the Group of Seven (G7) nations on currencies, he said.</p>
</text>
